format deletes the HTML block. The three lines of the div are simply gone
from the output, and the two paragraphs around it close up as though the
author had never written it.

What it should do: emit the raw HTML block unchanged, the way every markdown
renderer does.

Cause: MarkdownBlock in Sources/MarkdownKit/MarkdownParser.swift has seven
cases, and none of them is html. parseNode falls into its `default` branch for
CMARK_NODE_HTML_BLOCK, finds the type string is not "table", and returns nil.
FormatCommand then rebuilds the document out of the blocks it got back, so a
block the parser never returned cannot be written out again. The same silent
drop applies to every node kind the enum has no case for. Fixing it needs a
block case that carries the literal text, plus a BlockFormatter arm that
writes that text out verbatim.
